Readme per la versione JSF 12 e Spring 4 

Il progetto originale rende possibile utilizzare all'interno del codice JSF le funzionalita' di spring-security attraverso la realizzazione di una taglib.
Per realizzare l'integrazione con spring-4, si e' dovuto estendere il progetto presistente che forniva supporto per le versioni spring-2/3 e jsf12/20. 

Eseguire le seguenti istruzioni:

1) vi pom.xml :

- modificare l'artifactId da

	<artifactId>facelets-taglib-jsf12-spring-3</artifactId>

a

	<artifactId>facelets-taglib-jsf12-spring-4</artifactId>

- modificare la descrizione del progetto da

	<name>Spring Security + JSF/Facelets Tag Library: JSF 1.2 + Spring 3</name>

a 
	
	<name>Spring Security + JSF/Facelets Tag Library: JSF 1.2 + Spring 4</name>

- modificare le seguenti dipendenze da

	<dependency>
          <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
          <artifactId>org.springframework.security.core</artifactId>
          <version>${spring-security-3-version}</version>
          <scope>provided</scope>
        </dependency>

        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
            <artifactId>org.springframework.security.web</artifactId>
            <version>${spring-security-3-version}</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>

a 

        <dependency>
          <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
          <artifactId>spring-security-core</artifactId>
          <version>${spring-security-4-version}</version>
          <scope>provided</scope>
        </dependency>

        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-security-web</artifactId>
            <version>${spring-security-4-version}</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
	
- modificare le seguenti dipendenze da:

	<dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-test</artifactId>
            <version>${spring-3-version}</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>

a:

        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-test</artifactId>
            <version>${spring-4-version}</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>

- aggiungere il plugin per la compilazione con Java7:

...
    <build>
      <plugins>
	
	<!-- Inserire come primo plugin -->
	<plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                <configuration>
                    <source>1.7</source>
                    <target>1.7</target>
                    <encoding>UTF-8</encoding>                    
                </configuration>
            </plugin>

...

- aggiungere i repository mvn per jboss:
...
    </build>

	<!-- Inserire alla fine del tag build -->
	<repositories>
                <repository>
                        <id>jboss-releases</id>
                        <url>https://repository.jboss.org/nexus/content/repositories/releases/</url>
                </repository>
                <repository>
                        <id>jboss-thirdparty-releases</id>
                        <url>https://repository.jboss.org/nexus/content/repositories/thirdparty-releases/</url>
                </repository>
	
	</repositories>
...

2) vi src/main/java/org/springframework/security/taglibs/facelets/SpringSecurityELLibrary.java

nel metodo "private static GrantedAuthority[] getUserAuthorities()" modificare la riga:

	Collection<GrantedAuthority> authorities = currentUser.getAuthorities();

in:

	Collection<? extends GrantedAuthority> authorities = currentUser.getAuthorities();

3) vi src/test/java/org/springframework/security/taglibs/facelets/SpringSecurityELLibraryTest.java

- aggiungere gli import:

import java.util.Collection;
import java.util.Collections;

- modificare l'import: 

	import org.springframework.security.core.authority.GrantedAuthorityImpl;

in:

	import org.springframework.security.core.authority.SimpleGrantedAuthority;


- modificare:

  private final GrantedAuthority ROLE_ADMIN = new GrantedAuthorityImpl("ROLE_ADMIN");
  private final GrantedAuthority ROLE_USER = new GrantedAuthorityImpl("ROLE_USER");

in:

  private final GrantedAuthority ROLE_ADMIN = new SimpleGrantedAuthority("ROLE_ADMIN");
  private final GrantedAuthority ROLE_USER = new SimpleGrantedAuthority("ROLE_USER");


- sostituire nel metodo public void setUp() il seguente blocco di istruzioni:

    @SuppressWarnings("deprecation")
    User principal = new User("username", "password",
    /* enabled */true,
    /* accountNonExpired */true,
    /* credentialsNonExpired */true,
    /* accountNonLocked */true, new GrantedAuthority[] { ROLE_ADMIN, ROLE_USER });


con:

    List<GrantedAuthority> lst = new ArrayList<GrantedAuthority>();
    
    lst.add(ROLE_ADMIN);
    lst.add(ROLE_USER);
    
	Collection<? extends GrantedAuthority> authorities = Collections.unmodifiableList(lst );

    User principal = new User("username", "password",
    /* enabled */true,
    /* accountNonExpired */true,
    /* credentialsNonExpired */true,
    /* accountNonLocked */true, authorities);


- modificare il metodo private List<GrantedAuthority> getAnonymousAuthorities() sostituendo la riga:

	authorities.add(new GrantedAuthorityImpl("ROLE_ANONYMOUS"));

con:

	authorities.add(new SimpleGrantedAuthority("ROLE_ANONYMOUS"));

4) Ritornare al punto 8 del file README

